cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Telomere Evolution Lab"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alphine/telomore"
url: "https://studylab.id"
abstract: >-
  Telomere Evolution Lab is a stochastic, population-level simulator of
  telomere attrition, maintenance and replicative senescence, coupled to an
  evolutionary search over virtual experimental conditions. It is a
  hypothesis-generation and teaching tool, not a predictor: it is not fitted
  to patient data and is not intended for diagnosis or clinical use. Runs are
  reproducible from a seed and configuration through a run ledger.
keywords:
  - telomere
  - replicative senescence
  - computational biology
  - stochastic simulation
  - evolutionary algorithm
  - hypothesis generation
